ape & Layer","title":"Cream Butter & Sugar Fluffy","instructionTemplate":"Whisk the cream into stiff peaks. Carefully fold in the vanilla custard. Once the cake has cooled, cut it in half. You can use scissors for this, or a knife on a cutting board, slicing through the baking paper as well. Place half of the cake on a serving platter with the meringue side down and peel off the baking paper. Spread the cream filling across the cake. Then carefully remove the other half of the cake from the baking paper and place it over the cream filling, meringue side up.","durationMin":3,"timerSeconds":180,"activeMeasureSummary":"Milk, vanilla pod"},{"stepNumber":4,"phaseLabel":"Bake / Chill","title":"Cool, Garnish & Serve","instructionTemplate":"Serve with fresh berries. Plate into 6 generous servings while the flavors and textures are at their peak, and store any leftovers covered.","durationMin":30,"timerSeconds":1800,"activeMeasureSummary":"Butter, Granulated Sugar","criticalTip":"Let set for 5–10 minutes before slicing or plating so the textures hold crisp and photogenic!","creatorSecret":"Wait until the sponge feels cool to the touch before frosting so your glaze or cream stays thick and glossy."}],"ugcQuotes":[{"id":"muq-53128","handle":"@baker_kv-fjord","image":"./ai-images/kv-fjord-cake-verdens-beste-world-s-best-cake.jpg","quote":"Followed the scaled metric steps—came out flawless in 45 mins!","rating":5}]}}]
